<title>USA: TVA Watts Bar nuke trips off line -- NRC.</title>
<headline>TVA Watts Bar nuke trips off line -- NRC.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>TVA Nuclear's 1170 megawatt (MW) Watts Bar nuclear unit tripped off line early today due to low water levels in a steam generator, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;It tripped off line a little after five a.m. (0500 EST/1000 GMT). They were at 67 percent power,&quot; an NRC spokesman said.</p>
<p>The unit is located in Spring City, Tennessee.</p>
<p>No restart date was given.</p>
<p>As a matter of policy, TVA declines to comment on the status of its nuclear power plants.</p>
<p>((New York Power Desk 212-859-1624))</p>
</text>
